WEBVTT

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:16.030
Thank goodness!

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:18.120
They turned out beautiful.

00:01:54.090 --> 00:01:56.090
It seems no one's here yet.

00:01:57.220 --> 00:01:58.800
Then I can practice by myself.

00:02:07.270 --> 00:02:08.520
Marina-chan?

00:02:22.450 --> 00:02:23.410
I...

00:02:23.410 --> 00:02:24.700
Hadzuki-chan.

00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:27.870
Good morning.

00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:34.010
Every morning?

00:02:34.010 --> 00:02:34.880
Yeah.

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:38.350
I thought Seki-sensei was the one bringin' the flowers.

00:02:38.350 --> 00:02:40.600
I heard that Marina-chan is in the gardening club.

00:02:53.230 --> 00:02:56.280
Early Bird Marina and a Bouquet From the Heart.

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:12.540
Good morning.

00:03:13.170 --> 00:03:14.320
Are you going to practice today?

00:03:14.320 --> 00:03:15.170
Yes.

00:03:15.670 --> 00:03:19.380
The recital is on Sunday, so I want to practice more.

00:03:20.340 --> 00:03:22.340
This is the only time of day that the music room is available.

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:24.720
But, I didn't know that.

00:03:25.810 --> 00:03:28.520
I didn't know you play the violin, Hadzuki-chan.

00:03:28.520 --> 00:03:31.740
If I didn't come earlier, I wouldn't have known about you either.

00:03:31.740 --> 00:03:34.440
Marina-chan, you do so much for us.

00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:38.740
I'm going to the music room now.

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:41.280
Good luck!

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:42.200
Yup!

00:03:43.240 --> 00:03:45.070
Music Room

00:03:58.670 --> 00:04:01.590
Pretty Witchy Hadzuki-chi!

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:16.150
Paipai Ponpoi Puwapuwa Puu!

00:04:16.150 --> 00:04:19.610
Give me an audience to hear my playing!

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:33.120
Hmm... Even though I have to practice, I don't feel very enthusiastic at all.

00:04:35.330 --> 00:04:40.170
Because! I can't play well without any applause!

00:04:57.480 --> 00:05:01.430
Alright, open your textbooks to page 32.

00:05:01.430 --> 00:05:03.410
Sugiyama, read from the first line.

00:05:03.410 --> 00:05:04.450
Yes, ma'am.

00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:06.440
They're beautiful.

00:05:06.440 --> 00:05:07.950
Sweet peas, huh?

00:05:07.950 --> 00:05:11.910
Flowers... Flowers-are-beautiful.

00:05:12.660 --> 00:05:17.110
In-every-season...

00:05:17.110 --> 00:05:17.650
Koizumi.

00:05:17.650 --> 00:05:18.380
For-opening-up-our-hearts...

00:05:18.380 --> 00:05:20.590
Thank you for the flowers.

00:05:20.590 --> 00:05:21.590
For-opening-up-our-hearts...

00:05:25.760 --> 00:05:29.050
Is Seki-sensei thanking her for the flowers?

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:32.930
She must've known it was Marina-chan's work.

00:05:38.440 --> 00:05:39.360
Marina-chan!

00:05:42.070 --> 00:05:43.320
Ya look really into this!

00:05:44.110 --> 00:05:47.780
Ah, these look like they're about to bloom. What are they called?

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:50.410
Daisies, they're chrysanthemums.

00:05:50.410 --> 00:05:52.240
It means innocence in the flower language.

00:05:53.620 --> 00:05:55.240
You know so much about them!

00:05:55.240 --> 00:05:58.210
These are my favorite flowers.

00:06:04.170 --> 00:06:06.510
Hey! Harukaze!

00:06:07.720 --> 00:06:09.050
Could you throw me the ball?

00:06:10.090 --> 00:06:11.120
Kimura!

00:06:11.120 --> 00:06:12.680
How could you do this?

00:06:15.770 --> 00:06:18.560
You crushed her beautiful flowers!

00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:24.110
It's only some flowers, why are you getting all fired up about it?

00:06:24.110 --> 00:06:24.940
Right.

00:06:30.320 --> 00:06:33.280
I'm terribly sorry, huffyhuffy-huffy!

00:06:33.280 --> 00:06:36.740
Sure Doremi ain't so bright...

00:06:36.740 --> 00:06:39.040
Ai-chan, whose side are you on?

00:06:39.750 --> 00:06:40.540
Sorry.

00:06:41.750 --> 00:06:44.610
Marina-chan spent a lot of time taking care of those flowers!

00:06:44.610 --> 00:06:46.060
Yeah, apologize!

00:06:46.060 --> 00:06:46.710
Hurry!

00:06:49.880 --> 00:06:53.430
Why should I apologize to a teacher's pet?

00:06:54.930 --> 00:06:57.690
Kimura! How could you say that!?

00:06:57.690 --> 00:06:59.060
Well, it's true, isn't it?

00:07:00.980 --> 00:07:02.190
Marina-chan!

00:07:08.070 --> 00:07:09.030
Marina-chan!

00:07:12.950 --> 00:07:14.330
Don't mind what he said.

00:07:14.990 --> 00:07:16.450
No one believes you're a...

00:07:18.540 --> 00:07:19.830
Marina-chan?

00:07:28.590 --> 00:07:30.130
She's not here yet.

00:07:35.350 --> 00:07:38.920
Good morning!

00:07:44.360 --> 00:07:46.980
What happened to you today? Did you oversleep?

00:07:47.730 --> 00:07:48.990
I quit.

00:07:49.690 --> 00:07:53.410
I don't want to be the first one to class anymore.

00:07:54.910 --> 00:07:58.430
She's still shocked by Kimura's words.

00:07:58.430 --> 00:07:59.260
Looks like it.

00:08:06.250 --> 00:08:08.800
Jeez, this is all your fault, Kimura.

00:08:08.800 --> 00:08:12.550
55, 56, 57, 58...

00:08:12.550 --> 00:08:14.430
Don'tcha get it?

00:08:14.430 --> 00:08:16.930
A young girl's heart can be very delicate!

00:08:16.930 --> 00:08:20.930
What does it matter? Things are alright without the flowers.

00:08:32.950 --> 00:08:35.030
Aren't you attending your garden?

00:08:36.030 --> 00:08:41.760
No, Mom wanted me to come in early in the first place.

00:08:42.910 --> 00:08:46.710
My grades aren't especially good. And I don't do well in sports either.

00:08:46.710 --> 00:08:51.040
I'm not better than anyone else at anything.

00:08:51.710 --> 00:08:52.720
So...

00:08:53.380 --> 00:08:56.760
Well, how about you come in early every day?

00:08:57.470 --> 00:08:59.720
You like flowers, right?

00:08:59.720 --> 00:09:03.770
You can arrange the flowers every day and make the classroom a brighter place.

00:09:03.770 --> 00:09:06.730
Maybe the teachers will compliment you, too.

00:09:07.610 --> 00:09:10.340
I did that because Mom made me...

00:09:11.190 --> 00:09:12.100
But...

00:09:12.100 --> 00:09:13.400
That's why I quit!

00:09:13.400 --> 00:09:15.860
It's not that I like doing it anyway!

00:09:21.790 --> 00:09:23.910
So that's what Marina-chan said.

00:09:23.910 --> 00:09:27.520
What? Ain't she a teacher's pet like Kimura said?

00:09:27.520 --> 00:09:28.830
No, she isn't!

00:09:31.590 --> 00:09:35.760
I began taking violin lessons because my mama made me.

00:09:35.760 --> 00:09:38.760
I didn't like it at first, but now I think it's a lot of fun.

00:09:38.760 --> 00:09:40.890
So Marina-chan must feel the same way, too!

00:09:44.520 --> 00:09:45.680
What is it, Dodo?

00:09:49.060 --> 00:09:52.360
Dodo didn't used to like making magic goods?

00:09:54.780 --> 00:09:57.490
But since you're happy now, it's okay.

00:10:00.410 --> 00:10:04.360
You should've waited until you're better at making goods.

00:10:08.830 --> 00:10:09.850
A customer!

00:10:09.850 --> 00:10:11.240
Dodo, hide quickly!

00:10:16.090 --> 00:10:16.840
Kimura?

00:10:17.470 --> 00:10:18.130
Yo.

00:10:18.930 --> 00:10:20.050
What are you doing here?

00:10:20.050 --> 00:10:24.770
I-I happened to pass by, so I came in to check it out.

00:10:25.470 --> 00:10:29.100
Some strange stuff you have here.

00:10:29.100 --> 00:10:31.490
We don't have any magic goods for you.

00:10:31.490 --> 00:10:33.730
What did you say? I am a customer!

00:10:33.730 --> 00:10:36.940
Of course! And the customer is always right!

00:10:37.530 --> 00:10:39.610
As expected from a Naniwa personality...

00:10:39.610 --> 00:10:41.550
Is there anything botherin' ya?

00:10:41.550 --> 00:10:43.610
Well, uhm... Actually...

00:10:43.610 --> 00:10:46.320
Do you want to play soccer better?

00:10:46.320 --> 00:10:47.120
Of course not.

00:10:47.120 --> 00:10:50.790
Or is it a problem with a lover?

00:10:51.580 --> 00:10:54.800
Waaaaah! No way!

00:10:57.840 --> 00:10:58.760
How much is this!?

00:10:58.760 --> 00:11:00.760
Alright! Sold!

00:11:02.090 --> 00:11:02.640
Five yen.

00:11:03.640 --> 00:11:05.260
Come again...

00:11:07.060 --> 00:11:10.460
Hey, hey! He bought the magic goods Dodo made, didn't he?

00:12:18.380 --> 00:12:24.890
Hey Rere, is there any magic to help Marina-chan keep coming in early and arranging flowers every day?

00:12:26.470 --> 00:12:27.810
I guess not...

00:12:30.430 --> 00:12:31.300
That's it.

00:12:42.070 --> 00:12:45.570
Koizumi

00:12:46.530 --> 00:12:48.790
Yes, who is it?

00:12:48.790 --> 00:12:52.250
Uhm, I'm Fujiwara Hadzuki of class 3-2.

00:12:52.250 --> 00:12:54.860
Ah! Thank you for being such a good friend to Marina.

00:12:54.860 --> 00:12:56.000
One moment please.

00:12:56.540 --> 00:12:59.040
Marina, your friend is here for you.

00:13:01.590 --> 00:13:06.620
Wow! They're so pretty! These must be Marina-chan's work, too.

00:13:08.050 --> 00:13:08.890
Good morning.

00:13:11.350 --> 00:13:14.350
I thought we could go to school together.

00:13:16.230 --> 00:13:17.770
Mind your own business.

00:13:18.650 --> 00:13:19.570
Leave me alone!

00:13:34.830 --> 00:13:36.790
What should I do?

00:13:36.790 --> 00:13:40.180
Can't magic do anything about people's spirit?

00:13:45.670 --> 00:13:47.420
What a strong wind!

00:13:47.420 --> 00:13:49.380
It sure is!

00:14:01.440 --> 00:14:04.650
The weather report said it would rain.

00:14:15.080 --> 00:14:17.160
Wow. It's really pouring!

00:14:17.160 --> 00:14:19.000
Let's get goin' quickly.

00:14:19.000 --> 00:14:19.540
Yeah.

00:14:20.080 --> 00:14:21.750
Hadzuki-chan, let's go.

00:14:22.710 --> 00:14:24.340
Uhm, I have something to take care of.

00:14:27.930 --> 00:14:30.540
I'm sorry, I'm going home with Marina-chan today.

00:14:31.680 --> 00:14:32.470
I see.

00:14:32.470 --> 00:14:33.400
Okay then...

00:14:33.400 --> 00:14:34.430
See ya tomorrow.

00:14:35.640 --> 00:14:39.810
Dangit! Stupid wind, don't underestimate me!

00:14:46.740 --> 00:14:48.780
You don't have to do that.

00:14:51.620 --> 00:14:54.280
I'm not doing it for you, Koizumi.

00:14:54.280 --> 00:14:57.500
This garden has nothing to do with me anymore.

00:14:58.660 --> 00:14:59.620
Marina-chan...

00:15:03.880 --> 00:15:06.130
Kimura-kun, you're all wet.

00:15:06.760 --> 00:15:07.460
I'm alright.

00:15:19.100 --> 00:15:20.480
Kimura-kun, are you alright?

00:15:21.730 --> 00:15:22.560
Kimura-kun!

00:15:24.270 --> 00:15:25.860
You have a fever!

00:15:28.440 --> 00:15:29.190
Fujiwara.

00:15:30.540 --> 00:15:34.060
The magic goods you sold didn't work at all.

00:15:35.740 --> 00:15:41.460
I was hoping Koizumi'd come in early and arrange the flowers as usual.

00:15:41.960 --> 00:15:47.420
But won't the flowers be ruined with such a heavy rain?

00:15:47.420 --> 00:15:49.160
Kimura-kun...

00:15:49.160 --> 00:15:52.680
So you do care about what happens to Marina-chan.

00:15:54.560 --> 00:15:56.880
Oh my, you're still here?

00:15:58.270 --> 00:15:59.980
Yuki-sensei.

00:15:59.980 --> 00:16:02.940
Seki-sensei said she'd take Kimura-kun home.

00:16:02.940 --> 00:16:06.000
Don't worry, you can go home now.

00:16:06.000 --> 00:16:06.730
Yes.

00:16:06.730 --> 00:16:10.690
Be careful on the way. It's a storm out there.

00:16:11.650 --> 00:16:14.870
It's so rare to see such a big storm in spring.

00:16:39.520 --> 00:16:41.310
No, please hang in there.

00:16:42.060 --> 00:16:45.650
Kimura-kun protected the flowers with all his might.

00:16:46.230 --> 00:16:49.610
And Marina-chan's expecting them to bloom.

00:16:50.400 --> 00:16:51.440
If this keeps up...

00:17:07.920 --> 00:17:10.210
Pretty Witchy Hadzuki-chi!

00:17:11.760 --> 00:17:16.220
Paipai Ponpoi Puwapuwa Puu!

00:17:16.220 --> 00:17:18.220
Make the storm stop!

00:17:23.850 --> 00:17:27.770
I guess it's impossible for a level 9 apprentice to control nature...

00:17:28.650 --> 00:17:30.020
Alright, in that case...

00:17:31.110 --> 00:17:35.490
Paipai Ponpoi Puwapuwa Puu!

00:17:35.490 --> 00:17:37.820
Mini greenhouse, come out!

00:17:41.450 --> 00:17:44.660
Yay, yay, yay!

00:17:48.540 --> 00:17:50.090
This didn't work either...

00:17:50.710 --> 00:17:52.220
What am I going to do?

00:17:53.130 --> 00:17:54.010
Marina!

00:17:55.050 --> 00:17:58.380
It's too dangerous to go to school now! Stop it!

00:17:58.380 --> 00:17:59.010
But...!

00:18:01.050 --> 00:18:03.810
See! What if you get hurt?

00:18:12.730 --> 00:18:13.480
Rere!

00:18:16.400 --> 00:18:17.900
Are you here to get me?

00:18:19.240 --> 00:18:20.620
Thank you.

00:18:20.620 --> 00:18:21.870
Not just Rere.

00:18:21.870 --> 00:18:23.620
We're here to get ya, too.

00:18:24.290 --> 00:18:25.040
Doremi-chan!

00:18:25.040 --> 00:18:26.200
Ai-chan!

00:18:26.200 --> 00:18:29.460
I called you at home, but you weren't back yet.

00:18:29.460 --> 00:18:31.200
I thought you might still be at school.

00:18:31.200 --> 00:18:34.340
We thought maybe somethin' was buggin' ya.

00:18:34.340 --> 00:18:36.630
I'm so glad that you girls came!

00:18:36.630 --> 00:18:39.800
I can't protect the flowers with my magic alone.

00:18:40.340 --> 00:18:42.680
Please, lend me your power.

00:18:42.680 --> 00:18:44.550
We're going to use Magical Stage, right?

00:18:44.550 --> 00:18:45.390
No problem.

00:18:45.390 --> 00:18:47.350
Then, let's go.

00:18:47.890 --> 00:18:49.980
Pirika Pirilala Carefreely!

00:18:51.810 --> 00:18:54.900
Paipai Ponpoi Flexibly!

00:18:56.320 --> 00:18:59.200
Pameruku Laruku Proudly!

00:19:01.320 --> 00:19:02.820
Magical Stage!

00:19:09.580 --> 00:19:12.330
Please! Protect these flowers!

00:19:19.970 --> 00:19:22.760
What? There are so many mini-umbrellas.

00:19:26.180 --> 00:19:27.730
I see now.

00:19:27.730 --> 00:19:29.430
They're covering the flowers.

00:20:04.470 --> 00:20:05.940
Thank goodness....

00:20:05.940 --> 00:20:07.310
They're blooming.

00:20:07.310 --> 00:20:08.560
They're really blooming.

00:20:09.310 --> 00:20:10.140
Good morning.

00:20:11.140 --> 00:20:15.110
You did care. That's why you come in so early.

00:20:17.570 --> 00:20:18.440
They're so pretty.

00:20:19.400 --> 00:20:23.490
The flowers are blooming because Kimura-kun protected them.

00:20:24.280 --> 00:20:28.450
I started to come in early because Mom told me to do so at first.

00:20:28.450 --> 00:20:32.290
But I eventually grew to like it, which is why I came in early every day.

00:20:33.000 --> 00:20:36.330
It's because I love the morning air, I love the flowers.

00:20:36.330 --> 00:20:39.710
I love the shining desks under the morning light.

00:20:39.710 --> 00:20:41.330
Yeah, I understand.

00:20:41.330 --> 00:20:45.720
Actually, in the beginning, my mama also wanted me to learn the violin.

00:20:46.930 --> 00:20:48.430
I didn't say it yet.

00:20:48.430 --> 00:20:49.390
Say what?

00:20:50.180 --> 00:20:51.060
Good morning.

00:20:53.310 --> 00:20:54.140
Let's go to the classroom.

00:20:58.570 --> 00:21:01.420
I love the warm futon.

00:21:01.420 --> 00:21:03.520
I love having breakfast without pressure.

00:21:03.520 --> 00:21:06.360
But I love thick and juicy steak more.

00:21:06.360 --> 00:21:07.280
Right, right!

00:21:14.660 --> 00:21:17.130
Kimura

00:21:20.750 --> 00:21:21.800
Koizumi!

00:21:22.550 --> 00:21:24.380
I heard you caught a cold.

00:21:24.380 --> 00:21:29.300
It's not very serious. Mom just wants me to rest at home.

00:21:29.300 --> 00:21:31.470
For... for me?

00:21:32.850 --> 00:21:34.100
They bloomed this morning.

00:21:37.150 --> 00:21:38.730
It's really pretty.

00:21:39.360 --> 00:21:40.070
What's it called?

00:21:40.650 --> 00:21:41.360
It's a daisy.

00:21:44.440 --> 00:21:46.300
Hey hey. How was it?

00:21:46.300 --> 00:21:48.380
Doremi-chan, don't push.

00:21:48.380 --> 00:21:50.620
But I can't see.

00:22:02.000 --> 00:22:03.670
Hey wait! That's impossible!

00:22:03.670 --> 00:22:06.620
Pop's friend, Misaki-kun's wish...

00:22:06.620 --> 00:22:10.820
He wants his brother on the bench to play in the soccer game.

00:22:10.820 --> 00:22:12.890
It's pitiful, but it doesn't seem possible at all...

00:22:12.890 --> 00:22:15.520
We can't help him when he ain't got any skill!

00:22:15.520 --> 00:22:20.770
But we have to make him play for the goods Misaki-kun bought!

00:22:21.900 --> 00:22:23.150
Ojamajo Doremi!

00:22:23.150 --> 00:22:24.900
A Wish for a Precious Shirt.

00:22:25.690 --> 00:22:28.070
Happy! Lucky! For all of you!
